@testray.main.component.name = "Patcher Builder"
Feature: Patcher Builder and 72 builds
  	Testing creation of 72 builds on Patcher Builder.
  
  Setup:
  	* I go to the Patcher Builder Jenkins homepage

  Scenario: Run fix pack builder hotfix 7x job
    As a TSE, I should be able to run the fixpack-builder-hotfix-7x job

    Given I start the fixpack-builder-hotfix-7x job with the following parameters
      | fix.pack.customer.ticket         | 12345                                    |
      | fix.pack.built.for               | LIFEBENELUX                              |
      | fix.pack.fixed.issues            | LPE-0                                    |
      | fix.pack.hotfixed.issues         | LPSQA-122640,LPSQA-94011                 |
      | fix.pack.id                      | 894                                      |
      | git.revision                     | 191ab9558d9f1ecdbcccaa2534aad83d57879063 |
      | patcher.build.id                 | 180081960                                |
      | patcher.combined.branch          | true                                     |
      | patcher.user.id                  | 10196                                    |
      | patcher.fix.delivery.method      | Fix Pack 3.0                             |
      | release.tool.git.remote.username | eszterdudasschveder                      |
      | release.tool.git.branch          | LPS-122640-dxp8                          |
      | fix.pack.baseCommittish          | fix-pack-dxp-8-7210                      |
      | patcher.security.patch           | false                                    |
    And I wait for "5" seconds
    And I go to the Patcher Builder Jenkins homepage
    And I get the current build number for the job titled "fixpack-builder-hotfix-7x(2x-uat)"
    And I check the job with the name "fixpack-builder-hotfix-7x(2x-uat)" and build number "${staticJobBuildNumber}" for completion
    And I go to the Patcher Builder Jenkins homepage
    Then the job with the name "fixpack-builder-hotfix-7x(2x-uat)" and build number "${staticJobBuildNumber}" should have been successful

  Scenario: Run test fix pack builder install job
    As a TSE, I should be able to run the test-fixpack-builder-install job

    Given I start the test-fixpack-builder-install job with the following parameters
      | bundle                   | /mnt/mfs-hdd1-172.16.168/ee/portal/7.2.10/liferay-dxp-tomcat-7.2.10-ga1-20190531140450482.7z                                            |
      | fixPack                  | /mnt/mfs-hdd1-172.16.168/ee/fix-packs/7.2.10/dxp/liferay-fix-pack-dxp-8-7210.zip                                                        |
      | hotfix                   | /mnt/mfs-hdd1-10.50.0.33/live/opt/java/jenkins/userContent/liferay-fix-pack-builder/fix-packs/7.2.10/hotfix/liferay-hotfix-894-7210.zip |
      | patchingTool             | /mnt/mfs-hdd1-172.16.168/ee/fix-packs/patching-tool/patching-tool-LATEST.zip                                                            |
      | patchingToolMajorVersion | 2                                                                                                                                       |
    And I wait for "5" seconds
    And I go to the Patcher Builder Jenkins homepage
    And I get the current build number for the short job titled "test-fixpack-builder-install(2x-uat)"
    And I wait for "4" minutes
    And I stop the job titled "test-fixpack-builder-install(2x-uat)"
    And I go to the Patcher Builder Jenkins homepage
    And I go to the console output for the job with the name "test-fixpack-builder-install(2x-uat)" and build number "${staticJobBuildNumber}"
    Then the test-fixpack-builder-install console log should not have any visible errors

  Scenario: Run test fix pack builder revert job
    As a TSE, I should be able to run the test-fixpack-builder-revert job

    Given I start the test-fixpack-builder-revert job with the following parameters
      | bundle                   | /mnt/mfs-hdd1-172.16.168/ee/portal/7.2.10/liferay-dxp-tomcat-7.2.10-ga1-20190531140450482.7z                                            |
      | fixPack                  | /mnt/mfs-hdd1-172.16.168/ee/fix-packs/7.2.10/dxp/liferay-fix-pack-dxp-8-7210.zip                                                        |
      | hotfix                   | /mnt/mfs-hdd1-10.50.0.33/live/opt/java/jenkins/userContent/liferay-fix-pack-builder/fix-packs/7.2.10/hotfix/liferay-hotfix-894-7210.zip |
      | patchingTool             | /mnt/mfs-hdd1-172.16.168/ee/fix-packs/patching-tool/patching-tool-LATEST.zip                                                            |
      | patchingToolMajorVersion | 2                                                                                                                                       |
    And I wait for "5" seconds
    And I go to the Patcher Builder Jenkins homepage
    And I get the current build number for the short job titled "test-fixpack-builder-revert(2x-uat)"
    And I wait for "4" minutes
    And I stop the job titled "test-fixpack-builder-revert(2x-uat)"
    And I go to the Patcher Builder Jenkins homepage
    And I go to the console output for the job with the name "test-fixpack-builder-revert(2x-uat)" and build number "${staticJobBuildNumber}"
    Then the test-fixpack-builder-revert console log should not have any visible errors

  Scenario: Run test fix pack builder patch difference job
    As a TSE, I should be able to run the test-fixpack-builder-patch-difference job

    Given I start the test-fixpack-builder-patch-difference job with the following parameters
      | alphaPath | /mnt/mfs-hdd1-10.50.0.33/live/opt/java/jenkins/userContent/liferay-fix-pack-builder-backup/fix-packs/7.2.10/hotfix/liferay-hotfix-894-7210-alpha.zip |
      | betaPath  | /tmp/jenkins/cloud-10-50-0-133/fixpack-builder-hotfix-7x(2x-uat)/latest-hotfix/liferay-hotfix-894-7210.zip                                           |
    And I wait for "5" seconds
    And I go to the Patcher Builder Jenkins homepage
    And I get the current build number for the short job titled "test-fixpack-builder-patch-difference(2x-uat)"
    And I check the job with the name "test-fixpack-builder-patch-difference(2x-uat)" and build number "${staticJobBuildNumber}" for completion
    And I go to the Patcher Builder Jenkins homepage
    Then the job with the name "test-fixpack-builder-patch-difference(2x-uat)" and build number "${staticJobBuildNumber}" should have been successful
    When I go to the Patcher Builder Jenkins homepage
    And I go to the console output for the job with the name "test-fixpack-builder-patch-difference(2x-uat)" and build number "${staticJobBuildNumber}"
    Then the test-fixpack-builder-patch-difference console log should not have any visible errors

  Scenario: Save current hotfix
    As a TSE, I should be able to run the test-fixpack-builder-hotfix-copy job

    Given I start the test-fixpack-builder-hotfix-copy job with the following parameters
      | destinationFilePath | /mnt/mfs-hdd1-10.50.0.33/live/opt/java/jenkins/userContent/liferay-fix-pack-builder-backup/fix-packs/7.2.10/hotfix/liferay-hotfix-894-7210-alpha.zip |
      | originFilePath      | /tmp/jenkins/cloud-10-50-0-133/fixpack-builder-hotfix-7x(2x-uat)/latest-hotfix/liferay-hotfix-894-7210.zip                                           |
    And I wait for "5" seconds
    And I go to the Patcher Builder Jenkins homepage
    And I get the current build number for the short job titled "test-fixpack-builder-hotfix-copy(2x-uat)"
    And I check the job with the name "test-fixpack-builder-hotfix-copy(2x-uat)" and build number "${staticJobBuildNumber}" for completion
    And I go to the Patcher Builder Jenkins homepage
    Then the job with the name "test-fixpack-builder-hotfix-copy(2x-uat)" and build number "${staticJobBuildNumber}" should have been successful
